le thing he's been through it's  just just falling off as he goes north I  could go on about this for us John  belongs north of the wall all right now  let's break it down let's talk about  what he said first which is him saying  he has yet to watch the final episode  I'm sure some of you might be wondering  why that is well to be honest there are  always a number of different reasons why  some actors may never watch their own  work however we may already know why kid  Harrington decided not to revisit  Westeros after the show ended it might  still be too emotional for him if you  remember right after HBO released their  documentary on the  making of the final-season Herrington  actually checked himself into a wellness  facility for some much-needed therapy  there were many articles written on this  at the time as well a friend of the  actor added that the end of the  decade-long show really hit kid hard in  his wife fellow Game of Thrones actress  Rose Leslie was being extremely  supportive the Thrones documentary the  last watch was also released Sunday that  showed Harrington crying in dismay when  he first learned that his character Jon  Snow would kill the show's female lead  Daenerys Targaryen the actor also told  Esquire in April that he broke down  after shooting his final scenes as the  character the final day of shooting I  felt fine I felt fine I felt fine they  don't want to do my last shots and  started hyperventilating a bit then they  called a wrap and I just broke down it  was this onslaught of relief and grief  about not being able to do this again  now this is just a guess  but I think this might have something to  do with the fact that he has yet to  watch the final episode it's too  emotional for him and I would completely  understand if that were the case the  show had been a part of his life for  nearly a decade and not only that but  this was also the show that made his  career and completely changed his life  for better or worse he had also b